{
  "$comment": [
    "THE ASSET TYPE REGISTRY — the single definition of what kinds of thing this product can air.",
    "docs/asset-type-fixed-vs-configurable-2026-08-26.md · docs/library-asset-build-plan-2026-08-26.md",
    "",
    "ONE FILE, TWO LOADERS. src/lib/assetTypes.ts (renderer) and electron/asset-types.js (main +",
    "daemon) both read THIS data. Never two definitions — a type that existed in one and not the other",
    "is how a row becomes invisible to half the product.",
    "",
    "STRUCTURAL fields sit at the top level: code, badge, colours, commercial, metaTable. They are the",
    "same on every station and are NOT overridable — `logsAs` is the code itself, and the as-run record",
    "must mean the same thing everywhere or no cross-station report can be trusted.",
    "",
    "`defaults` are OPERATOR-CONFIGURABLE per station, overridden in station_config_kv under",
    "asset_type.<CODE>.<behaviour>. The registry says how a type behaves by default; the operator",
    "decides how THEIR station runs. An absent override means 'use the default' — never false.",
    "",
    "DUCKING IS DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Duck is a function of the CHANNEL/DECK, available to anything",
    "loaded on it including a live mic. Nothing here may override, replace, gate or pre-empt it.",
    "",
    "ADDING A TYPE = ADDING AN OBJECT HERE. No migration (library_asset.type has no CHECK constraint),",
    "no edits to rotation, the scheduler, the log generator or the UI. That is the acceptance criterion,",
    "and assetTypes.test.ts asserts it by registering a fake type and checking it appears everywhere."
  ],

